{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRouterState"},{"type":"text","value":" method is a hook that returns the current internal state of the router. This hook is useful for accessing the current state of the router in a component."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Tip","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to access the current location or the current matches, you should try out the "},{"type":"link","href":"./useLocationHook.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLocation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"./useMatchesHook.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMatches"}]},{"type":"text","value":" hooks first. These hooks are designed to be more performant, more ergonomic and easier to use than accessing the router state directly."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"userouterstate-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useRouterState options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRouterState"},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"opts-select-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opts.select"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(state: RouterState) => TSelected"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If supplied, this function will be called with the "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouterStateType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouterState"}]},{"type":"text","value":" object and the return value will be returned from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRouterState"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"opts-structuralsharing-option","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opts.structuralSharing"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configures whether structural sharing is enabled for the value returned by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guide/render-optimizations.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render Optimizations guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"userouterstate-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useRouterState returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The current "},{"type":"link","href":"./RouterStateType.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RouterState"}]},{"type":"text","value":" object or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" if a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" function is provided."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRouterState } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n  //    ^ RouterState\n\n  // OR\n\n  const selected = useRouterState({\n    select: (state) => state.location,\n  })\n  //    ^ ParsedLocation\n\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"userouterstate-options","text":"useRouterState options","level":2},{"id":"opts-select-option","text":"opts.select option","level":3},{"id":"opts-structuralsharing-option","text":"opts.structuralSharing option","level":3},{"id":"userouterstate-returns","text":"useRouterState returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `useRouterState` method is a hook that returns the current internal state of the router. This hook is useful for accessing the current state of the router in a component.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you want to access the current location or the current matches, you should try out the [`useLocation`](./useLocationHook.md) and [`useMatches`](./useMatchesHook.md) hooks first. These hooks are designed to be more performant, more ergonomic and easier to use than accessing the router state directly.\n\n## useRouterState options\n\nThe `useRouterState` hook accepts an optional `options` object.\n\n### `opts.select` option\n\n- Type: `(state: RouterState) => TSelected`\n- Optional\n- If supplied, this function will be called with the [`RouterState`](./RouterStateType.md) object and the return value will be returned from `useRouterState`.\n\n### `opts.structuralSharing` option\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional\n- Configures whether structural sharing is enabled for the value returned by `select`.\n- See the [Render Optimizations guide](../../guide/render-optimizations.md) for more information.\n\n## useRouterState returns\n\n- The current [`RouterState`](./RouterStateType.md) object or `TSelected` if a `select` function is provided.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRouterState } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n  //    ^ RouterState\n\n  // OR\n\n  const selected = useRouterState({\n    select: (state) => state.location,\n  })\n  //    ^ ParsedLocation\n\n  // ...\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useRouterStateHook\ntitle: useRouterState hook\n---\n\nThe `useRouterState` method is a hook that returns the current internal state of the router. This hook is useful for accessing the current state of the router in a component.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you want to access the current location or the current matches, you should try out the [`useLocation`](./useLocationHook.md) and [`useMatches`](./useMatchesHook.md) hooks first. These hooks are designed to be more performant, more ergonomic and easier to use than accessing the router state directly.\n\n## useRouterState options\n\nThe `useRouterState` hook accepts an optional `options` object.\n\n### `opts.select` option\n\n- Type: `(state: RouterState) => TSelected`\n- Optional\n- If supplied, this function will be called with the [`RouterState`](./RouterStateType.md) object and the return value will be returned from `useRouterState`.\n\n### `opts.structuralSharing` option\n\n- Type: `boolean`\n- Optional\n- Configures whether structural sharing is enabled for the value returned by `select`.\n- See the [Render Optimizations guide](../../guide/render-optimizations.md) for more information.\n\n## useRouterState returns\n\n- The current [`RouterState`](./RouterStateType.md) object or `TSelected` if a `select` function is provided.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRouterState } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const state = useRouterState()\n  //    ^ RouterState\n\n  // OR\n\n  const selected = useRouterState({\n    select: (state) => state.location,\n  })\n  //    ^ ParsedLocation\n\n  // ...\n}\n```\n"}
